FIX LINE-PRIM SIGNATURE (wasm): FE menu line prims trapped call_indirect

FUN_00412694 (LINE-prim rasterizer, _primfuncs type 0x42) is declared with one
parameter; _ot_dispatch calls every prim handler as (prim,b,c). Native cdecl
ignores the extra args; wasm's call_indirect type check traps ("function
signature mismatch"). The front end is the first path that draws line prims
(menu underlines via Draw_Screen_Lines), so the browser/node 'fe' boot died on
its first menu frame (localized with the new DD2_OTLOG: last dispatch t=42
fn=table-index-31). Normalized to the dispatch shape with unused extra params,
like the strip-trigger table (FUN_00448e50) and subdiv dispatch (610) cases.

--- a/dd2.c
+++ b/dd2.c
@@ -26,7 +26,7 @@
 void FUN_00411e0c(int _p1,int _p2,int param_1);
 void __cdecl FUN_00411ebc(int *param_1,undefined *param_2);
 void __cdecl FUN_0041243c(int *param_1,undefined *param_2);
-void __cdecl FUN_00412694(int param_1);
+void __cdecl FUN_00412694(int param_1,int _ot_b,int _ot_c);  /* patch 765: call_indirect signature normalization */
 void __cdecl ClearOTagR(undefined4 *param_1,int param_2);
 void __cdecl DrawOTag(int *param_1);
 void __cdecl DrawPrim(int param_1);
@@ -2584,9 +2584,16 @@
 
